            <ArticleTitle>Vaginal laceration and perforation resulting from first coitus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>113-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Vaginal laceration resulting from coitus is not uncommon and is well described. Perforation of the vagina during coitus is a very rare occurrence, and there is scant literature reporting it. This is a case of a 14-year-old female who suffered both laceration and perforation of the vagina as a result of her first coitus, which was consensual. The characteristics of vaginal laceration and perforation, presentation, treatment, complications, as well as predisposing factors, are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
